(Bug #14 regression, shape A: each `but if` branch is a fallible action
followed by its own `On error` handler, so each branch's own period closes
only that `On error` sentence -- not the whole chain. Every branch must get
its chance to fire, not just the first.)

a list called fs is ["proc", "sysfs", "tmpfs", "other"].
For each f in fs,
  Continue,
    but if f is equal to "proc" Open a file for reading called fa at "/nonexistent_dir/p", On error print "FAILED proc".
    but if f is equal to "sysfs" Open a file for reading called fb at "/nonexistent_dir/s", On error print "FAILED sysfs".
    but if f is equal to "tmpfs" Open a file for reading called fc at "/nonexistent_dir/t", On error print "FAILED tmpfs".

Print "done".
